# Redirects for mayongbesttantrik.com
#
# Workers static assets only. Cloudflare's docs are explicit that domain-level
# redirects are NOT supported here ("Domain-level redirects: no"), and the
# wrangler deploy fails outright on an absolute source:
#
#     Invalid _redirects configuration:
#     Line 36: Only relative URLs are allowed. [code: 100324]
#
# So the www and http rules that used to be in this file cannot live here. They
# are a Cloudflare Redirect Rule in the dashboard, which runs in front of the
# Worker - see worker.js for why that matters.
#
# Every rule below is a relative path redirect with an explicit 301. Workers
# defaults to 302 when the code is omitted, which is the same authority-
# withholding problem as the 307 this replaces: a 302 or 307 tells Google the
# move is temporary, so the clean URL never inherits the .html one.
#
# The three defects these fix, all measured on the live host:
#
#   1. /about.html answered 307 to /about, withholding authority permanently.
#   2. /about/ and /file/index also answered 307.
#   3. www 404'd and http:// served 200, both now handled in the Worker.

# index.html and hi/index.html are listed first and separately. The /*.html
# rule below would send /index.html to /index and /hi/index.html to /hi/index,
# neither of which exists.
/index.html      /          301
/hi/index.html   /hi/       301

/*.html          /:splat    301

# 404.html is deliberately absent. It is the filename not_found_handling looks
# for when it renders an error, and it has to keep existing at exactly that
# path - a rule moving it would move the error handler itself.
